      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right to push past the \"tension\" argument because many scholars classify targeted sanctions that ignore civilian suffering as a form of state-sponsored violence rather than legitimate diplomacy. Framing truth as a strategic objective becomes morally problematic when the primary mechanism of coercion directly infringes on human rights and averages life expectancy drops among the vulnerable. While realist theories often prioritize regime change, a democratic IR class paper would likely conclude that strategies causing widespread starvation fail the ethical test necessary for any policy claiming to promote democracy.",
